WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.541
(playful guitar music)

00:00:01.541 --> 00:00:03.039
- [Narrator] Jeju is a volcanic island

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:04.739
off the coast of South Korea,

00:00:04.739 --> 00:00:06.882
home to Hallasan, the highest mountain

00:00:06.882 --> 00:00:09.180
and dormant volcano in South Korea.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.510
The island was created entirely
from volcanic eruptions

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.820
two million years ago in the Cenozoic Era.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.514
Check out the island’s lava tubes.

00:00:18.514 --> 00:00:20.544
(playful music)

00:00:20.544 --> 00:00:23.153
The island is also home
to the grandfather stones,

00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:27.820
considered to be Gods offering
protection and fertility.

00:00:28.892 --> 00:00:32.518
As well as it's beautiful beaches.

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:33.851
And a love land.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.440
Let's leave them to it.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.656
The island is also home to a secret.

00:00:40.656 --> 00:00:42.604
The farm where Korean
Air grows and cultivates

00:00:42.604 --> 00:00:45.144
food for its first-class passengers.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.091
For years, Korean Air has operated

00:00:47.091 --> 00:00:49.216
Je-dong Farm on the island.

00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:52.192
The farm was originally opened
by the owners of Korean Air

00:00:52.192 --> 00:00:56.338
in 1972 when there was a
shortage of beef in Korea.

00:00:56.338 --> 00:00:58.330
Cattle were brought in to
help supply the country

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.797
but by the '90s, cows were everywhere,

00:01:00.797 --> 00:01:03.939
so the farm turned its attention
to more upmarket produce.

00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:06.523
Premium, environmentally-friendly beef.

00:01:06.523 --> 00:01:11.183
That's one happy cow. (cow moos)

00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:13.851
There are several barns holding
cows who will supply beef

00:01:13.851 --> 00:01:18.851
to Korean Air's first and
business-class passengers.

00:01:18.928 --> 00:01:21.497
There's also a very
large poultry population,

00:01:21.497 --> 00:01:23.263
and they roam free.

00:01:23.263 --> 00:01:24.341
(chickens clucking)

00:01:24.341 --> 00:01:25.501
The roosters?

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:29.101
Well, they're just hanging
out with the ladies.

00:01:29.101 --> 00:01:31.282
Peppers were hard to find in Korea,

00:01:31.282 --> 00:01:32.987
so the farm started growing their own

00:01:32.987 --> 00:01:36.654
using Jeju's clean,
volcanic artesian water.

00:01:37.792 --> 00:01:40.542
And these lovely cherry tomatoes.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.399
The island is also home to
the best groundwater in Korea.

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:48.270
Because of the layers of lava
flow and volcanic clusters,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.968
the island has very high water absorption.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.523
The water is withdrawn from
the ground and bottled here

00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:55.893
at the state-of-the-art production plant.

00:01:55.893 --> 00:01:58.379
Jeju Pure Water is clear
and clean mineral water

00:01:58.379 --> 00:02:01.664
containing organic components
so it's great for you.

00:02:01.664 --> 00:02:04.878
The water is also being
served on Korean Air flights.

00:02:04.878 --> 00:02:07.522
In Seoul, the Korean Air
chefs are cooking up a treat

00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:09.105
for the passengers.

00:02:10.303 --> 00:02:13.715
(playful music)

00:02:13.715 --> 00:02:15.661
Here, you can see some
of the hard work put in

00:02:15.661 --> 00:02:18.348
by the farm and the chickens.

00:02:18.348 --> 00:02:21.458
And how does it taste above the clouds?

00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.733
Excellent, of course.

00:02:23.733 --> 00:02:26.233
(sonar chime)

